{"name":"Black Power","hex":"#654b37","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Black Power","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slogan and  movement for self-determination for Black peoples.","A slogan or movement of separatism for Black communities in predominantly non-Black countries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Black_Power"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black power","blocks":[{"text":"Black power is a political slogan and a name which is given to various associated ideologies which aim to achieve self-determination for black people. It is primarily, but not exclusively, used in the United States by black activists and other proponents of what the slogan entails. The black power movement was prominent in the late 1960s and early 1970s, emphasizing racial pride and the creation of black political and cultural institutions to nurture, promote and advance what was seen by proponents of the movement as being the collective interests and values of Black Americans."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_power","wikidata":"Q880483"},{"title":"Black Power (New Zealand gang)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Power is a prominent gang in New Zealand. Members are predominantly Māori and Pasifika."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Power_(New_Zealand_gang)","wikidata":"Q4921495"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/John_Carlos%2C_Tommie_Smith%2C_Peter_Norman_1968cr.jpg/500px-John_Carlos%2C_Tommie_Smith%2C_Peter_Norman_1968cr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/John_Carlos%2C_Tommie_Smith%2C_Peter_Norman_1968cr.jpg/500px-John_Carlos%2C_Tommie_Smith%2C_Peter_Norman_1968cr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tommie Smith and John Carlos showing the raised fist on the podium after the 200 m race at the 1968 Summer Olympics","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohn_Carlos%2C_Tommie_Smith%2C_Peter_Norman_1968cr.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Ferguson%2C_Day_4%2C_Photo_21.png/500px-Ferguson%2C_Day_4%2C_Photo_21.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Ferguson%2C_Day_4%2C_Photo_21.png/500px-Ferguson%2C_Day_4%2C_Photo_21.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Protester raises his fist in black power salute, Ferguson, Missouri, 15 August 2014","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFerguson%2C_Day_4%2C_Photo_21.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Black_Lives_Matter_protest_%28first_debate_2016%29.jpg/500px-Black_Lives_Matter_protest_%28first_debate_2016%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Black_Lives_Matter_protest_%28first_debate_2016%29.jpg/1280px-Black_Lives_Matter_protest_%28first_debate_2016%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u